body:
After signup, users were returned to the previous screen without capturing preferences. This defers critical onboarding data collection to a later interaction that may never happen.

## Changes

### Modified signup flows to show preferences inline
- **`signup.js`**: Added `showPreferences` state flag to conditionally render `EditPreferences` after account creation
- **`SignUpPage.js`**: Same pattern applied to modal-based signup

Both implementations:
- Transition to preferences screen on successful signup instead of navigating back
- Pass default empty preferences to `EditPreferences` component
- Wrap `updatePreferences` to handle save + navigation
- Allow skip via close button (X)

```javascript
const onSignUp = async () => {
    // ... validation ...
    const result = await signUp(username, email, name, password);
    if (result) {
        setShowPreferences(true);  // Show preferences instead of router.back()
    }
}

if (showPreferences) {
    return <EditPreferences 
        userPreferences={defaultPrefs} 
        updatePreferences={handleSavePreferences} 
    />;
}
```

## User Flow
Signup form → Account created → **Preferences screen** → Save/Skip → Previous screen

