### Problem
Assessment gets stuck at "Calculating your IRL level..." screen and never redirects to results page.

### Root Causes
1. **Undefined `currentUser` variable** in `assessment-engine.js` could cause reference errors
2. **No error handling** in completion flow - errors fail silently

### Solutions

#### 1. Fixed `currentUser` Reference (`assessment-engine.js`)
```javascript
// Before (undefined variable)
userId: currentUser?.id,
userEmail: currentUser?.email

// After (safe null values with TODO)
userId: null, // TODO: Integrate with auth system
userEmail: null // TODO: Integrate with auth system
```

#### 2. Added Error Handling (`questions.html`)
```javascript
// Before (no error handling)
setTimeout(() => {
    assessmentEngine.calculateScores();
    assessmentEngine.saveAssessmentToStorage();
    window.location.href = 'results.html';
}, 2000);

// After (with try-catch and logging)
setTimeout(() => {
    try {
        console.log('Starting score calculation...');
        assessmentEngine.calculateScores();
        console.log('Scores calculated:', assessmentEngine.currentAssessment.scores);

        console.log('Saving assessment...');
        assessmentEngine.saveAssessmentToStorage();
        console.log('Assessment saved successfully');

        console.log('Redirecting to results...');
        window.location.href = 'results.html';
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Error completing assessment:', error);
        alert('Error saving assessment: ' + error.message);
    }
}, 2000);
```

